{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadPhaseAlgebra","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.WhiteheadPhaseAlgebra","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Knot.WhiteheadLinkScaffold"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.tendsto_center_linear_phase","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.tendsto_center_linear_phase","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadPhaseAlgebra.lean#L132-L143","doc":"The central linear phase itself: `exp(⌊N/2⌋πi/(2N)) → e^{iπ/4}` —\nthe constant vdV's `ψ = e^{(4a+3c−3d)πi/4}` absorbs at `Q_∞`\nassembly (Step 3). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.tendsto_center_linear_arg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.tendsto_center_linear_arg","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadPhaseAlgebra.lean#L94-L130","doc":"Along the central row `n = ⌊N/2⌋`, the linear phase argument\n`nπ/(2N)` tends to `π/4` (vdV: `lim n/(2N) = 1/4`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.tendsto_whiteheadLink_globalPhase","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.tendsto_whiteheadLink_globalPhase","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadPhaseAlgebra.lean#L67-L92","doc":"The Whitehead-link global phase `φ_N = e^{(N−1)πi/N}` tends to\n`e^{(c−d)πi} = −1` (vdV Step 3, `c − d = 1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadLinkPhase_decomp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadLinkPhase_decomp","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadPhaseAlgebra.lean#L45-L65","doc":"**L4-4 — the Fresnel-phase decomposition (sorry-free, exact).**  The\nscaffold's phase `χ_{N,n}^{−1}` factors as the pure Gaussian quadratic\n`exp(−n′²πi/(2N))` times the constant `e^{+Nπi/8}` times the linear\n`exp(−nπi/(2N))` — vdV Step 3, inverted to the scaffold convention. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadLinkPhase_arg_decomp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.whiteheadLinkPhase_arg_decomp","kind":"theorem","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/WhiteheadPhaseAlgebra.lean#L31-L43","doc":"The real-argument identity behind vdV's Step-3 phase split:\n`−n(n+1−N)/(2N) = −(n−N/2)²/(2N) + N/8 − n/(2N)` (times `π`) —\nnote the POSITIVE `N/8`: inverting vdV's `χ·e^{Nπi/8} = exp(n′²πi/(2N))\n·exp(nπi/(2N))` puts `e^{+Nπi/8}` on the `χ^{−1}` side. ","signatureChunk":0}]}